# Line endings are pinned to LF everywhere: in the repository and in the
# working tree, on every platform.
#
# This is not cosmetic. `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows checks files out as
# CRLF, while Cloudflare's Linux builder gets LF. Vue derives each component's
# scoped-style id (`data-v-…`) from its source bytes, so the same commit
# compiles to different ids — and therefore different asset content hashes —
# depending on which machine ran the build. That makes a local `npm run build`
# impossible to compare against what Workers Builds actually deployed, so
# "is production running this commit?" can't be answered from hashes alone.
#
# `eol=lf` is per-repo and overrides core.autocrlf, so this holds for anyone
# who clones the project regardless of their global git config.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries are exempt from all conversion. `text=auto` guesses most of these
# correctly on its own, but the tracked sqlite files under .wrangler/state and
# the .ico are exactly the cases where a wrong guess corrupts a file silently.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.webp          binary
*.avif          binary
*.ico           binary
*.pdf           binary

# Fonts.
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.ttf           binary
*.otf           binary
*.eot           binary

# Audio for the music player (public/music/).
*.mp3           binary
*.m4a           binary
*.ogg           binary
*.opus          binary
*.wav           binary
*.flac          binary

# Local miniflare dev state and Cygwin crash dumps. Both are matched by
# .gitignore but were committed before those rules existed, so they are still
# tracked and still need protecting from conversion.
*.sqlite        binary
*.sqlite-shm    binary
*.sqlite-wal    binary
*.stackdump     binary
